{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen","id":1507387,"title":"Magical doping for bodybuilders, powerlifters and strongmen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-04T03:14:24-07:00","id":1507387,"title":"Magical doping for bodybuilders, powerlifters and strongmen","content":"The supplement for Mage named &quot;Blood Treachery&quot; has an extremely intersting chapter about ghouls, although since it diverges a bit from other sources I don't know if it can be considered canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The powers easiest for vampires to learn are the physical ones. With time, the mage's strength may increase to superhuman levels. Ghoul mages also tend to become tougher than normal mortals. Better still, a mage who manages to survive quite a bit of punishment while &quot;under the blood&quot; may become so unnaturally resilient \u2014 i.e., his flesh may become so corpselike \u2014 that he can resist even Pattern damage. (In game terms, 76 Blood Treachery a mage can gain an extra soak die that's usable against any damage for 15 experience points. As long as a mage is a ghoul, he gains a full Stamina soak roll against lethal damage as well as bashing damage.) </div> </div> </div><br /> So, with time a ghoul ( here they talk about a ghoul mage but I think it applies to any ghoul ) may become superhumanly strong. But, rulewise, unless the Vitae comes from a low generation vampire, the ghoul is limited to one dot of Potence.<br /> Mabye this means a ghoul can become stronger ( in game terms: increase his Strength dots ) by learning to better use the power of Vitae, as a true vampire does. So, even a frail old man that becomes a ghoul and stay ghouled from decades may increase his Strength from 1 to 5, something that no amount of training and steroids would be normally able to accomplish... even if that increase is not, by RAW, superhuman or supernatural.<br /> <br /> I find expecially interesting the part &quot;Better still, a mage who manages to survive quite a bit of punishment while &quot;under the blood&quot; may become so unnaturally resilient \u2014 i.e., his flesh may become so corpselike \u2014 that he can resist even Pattern damage.&quot; . What does it mean exactly &quot;corpselike flesh&quot; in a living being like a ghoul? Since it's talking about unnatural resilience I guess its more &quot;leathery and wiry&quot; than &quot;pale and decomposed&quot;.<br /> Mabye, the more a ghoul regenerates wounds using the power of Vitae, the more his rebuilt flesh assumes the semblance of vampire flesh. Or mabye, he depends less and less on natural biology and more and more on the mystical power of Vitae, so he becomes able to soak lethal damage with his Stamina.<br /> <br /> <br /> Final note about bodybuilders ghouls: I have been said in a similar conversation that vampiric tendence toward stasis would means that regenerating micro-wounds caused by training using the power of Vitae would undue the ghoul's gains, since he would simply return to the previous state.<br /> Mabye it's true, mabye not, but for sure a ghoul - this is stated explicitly - has more energies and tires less quickly than a common mortal, so he would be able to exercise more and more easily.<br /> And, even if he doesn't use his healing power to recover from normal muscular stress, he would still be able to repair strains, tendon damage and other injuries when needed... and that would be an enormous boon for any bodybuilder.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Question 0: </i></b>should a ghoul get a small discount when buying Strength, Stamina or dots in Athletics to reflect those facilitations?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> <b><i>Question 1: </i></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With time, the mage's strength may increase to superhuman levels. Ghoul mages also tend to become tougher than normal mortals. </div> </div> </div>How would you convey that in the game, from a stats viewpoint? I don't think that extra dots of Potence and Resilience would be appropriate ( it would require an elder's Vitae source ).<br /> A modest discount on the xp cost for increasing Strength and Stamina, mabye?<br /> <br /> <b><i>Question 2: </i></b>Vicissitude tends to alter the body in a quite brutal, I would say &quot;surgically invasive&quot; way. There are any thaumaturgy or sorcerous paths or rituals / hedge magics / psionic powers\u200b that could allow a mortal to influence the production of testosterone, somatotropine, myostatine ecc. in order to grow a bigger, more muscular body in a slower and - hopefully - less traumatic way than Vicissitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-04-2023, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T07:58:20-07:00","id":1507404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen#post1507387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Question 0: </i></b>should a ghoul get a small discount when buying Strength, Stamina or dots in Athletics to reflect those facilitations?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, but a Merit for an aptitude would be ok, imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen#post1507387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Question 1: </i></b><br /> <br /> How would you convey that in the game, from a stats viewpoint? I don't think that extra dots of Potence and Resilience would be appropriate ( it would require an elder's Vitae source ).<br /> A modest discount on the xp cost for increasing Strength and Stamina, mabye?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly parse that quote as &quot;a ghoul can have Potence/Celerity/Fortitude and burn blood to increase physical attributes&quot; without using the splat-specific terminology. It's a Mage supplement after all.<br /> The sentence about being 'corpse-like' I interpret as more relevant to their magical pattern than perhaps their appearance. I could see a ghoul somewhat resistant to Life Sphere effects, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen#post1507387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <b><i>Question 2: </i></b>Vicissitude tends to alter the body in a quite brutal, I would say &quot;surgically invasive&quot; way. There are any thaumaturgy or sorcerous paths or rituals / hedge magics / psionic powers\u200b that could allow a mortal to influence the production of testosterone, somatotropine, myostatine ecc. in order to grow a bigger, more muscular body in a slower and - hopefully - less traumatic way than Vicissitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned in the other thread, the original version of Biothauma could be used. Although that Path was made for Frankenstein type experiments, so I'm not sure it would be less invasive than Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> Alchemy is great for this. You can create super-powered dietary supplements, salves etc that aid the natural gain like the mundane stuff would, only much more potent.<br /> <br /> There's Biocontrol as a psychic power, which is all about manipulating body drugs and agents. I also wouldn't mind Rituals for the Healing Sorcery Path that aim at building up physique. S20 has one example Ritual that is based on Humors.<br /> <br /> Sphere Magick of course is versatile enough to just do what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T08:29:31-07:00","id":1507409,"title":"","content":"I think I've read somewere about a kinda dumb technocrate who apported a lot of genetical changes to his body and was described as a &quot;shaved, oiled gorilla with white teeth and blonde hairs&quot;. He had Strength 7 and Stamina 6, or something similar. Can't remember the book.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Found it, it was Chaos Factor, a mage named Justin Wadsworth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-04-2023, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T00:05:27-07:00","id":1508120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen?p=1507409#post1507409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've read somewere about a kinda dumb technocrate who apported a lot of genetical changes to his body (...)<br /> <br /> Found it, it was Chaos Factor, a mage named Justin Wadsworth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew it had to be one of these books. Early MtA supplements used to contain many corrupt, extremist, or criminal characters who are hilarious or baffling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-12-2023, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T07:27:05-07:00","id":1508630,"title":"","content":"Some bits from <i>PANACEA Pharmaceuticals</i>, might help (some side effect to be expected).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T21:33:55-07:00","id":1509252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen?p=1507409#post1507409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've read somewere about a kinda dumb technocrate who apported a lot of genetical changes to his body and was described as a &quot;shaved, oiled gorilla with white teeth and blonde hairs&quot;. He had Strength 7 and Stamina 6, or something similar. Can't remember the book.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Found it, it was Chaos Factor, a mage named Justin Wadsworth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 24 in Book of Chantries also has a super ghoul mage, Klaus Hortemone, having Str 7, Dx 6, Sta 6, Melee 6 and Thaumaturgy 2<br /> <br /> Of course it\u2019s very old and no ghoul mage rules during that time, wonder if he was reset later<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1507387-magical-doping-for-bodybuilders-powerlifters-and-strongmen?p=1508120#post1508120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I knew it had to be one of these books. Early MtA supplements used to contain many corrupt, extremist, or criminal characters who are hilarious or baffling.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtA and MtA 1E is always much more goth punk, if you go into the Book of Chantries again, it\u2019s full of corrupt and intrigue<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-22-2023, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}